endobj

216 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(DESCRIPTION - CHAMBER CONSTRUCTION )/E(DESCRIPTION - CHAMBER CONSTRUCTION )/Pg 14 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

217 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(The chamber is meticulously crafted with a double-walled, insulated design using argon Tig/arc welded stainless steel sheet \(304\) measuring 1.5/1.2 mm in thickness for the interior, while the outer walls are constructed using CRCA, as specified in the customer's tender RFQ sheet, with a thickness of 1.5 mm. The outer body is manufactured using CNC technology, ensuring precise production and featuring seamlessly smooth joints without any protruding fixtures. )/Pg 14 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

218 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 35 0 R/Pg 14 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

219 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(The chamber's door is coated with an epoxy-based powder in RAL 9001 cream white, while the main chamber body is finished with RAL 7024 graphite grey powder coating. The chamber is ingeniously designed in a vertical trolley mounting configuration, featuring a fully frontal opening double-walled insulated door. This door is thoughtfully equipped with an exclusively sourced high-quality silicone rubber gasket for optimal sealing. To ensure both security and insulation, the door is fitted with robust hinges and a toggle-type locking mechanism.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

220 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(This meticulous attention to construction details not only underscores the chamber's durability and functionality but also enhances its aesthetic appeal.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

221 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(IN OUR CLIMATIC TEST CHAMBER'S AIR CIRCULATION SYSTEM, WE INCORPORATE THE FOLLOWING COMPONENTS AND FEATURES)/E(IN OUR CLIMATIC TEST CHAMBER'S AIR CIRCULATION SYSTEM, WE INCORPORATE THE FOLLOWING COMPONENTS AND FEATURES)/Pg 14 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

222 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Fan/Blower: The chamber is equipped with a fan or blower featuring a continuous-duty rated motor. This motor efficiently circulates air within the chamber.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

223 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Conditioning Space: Inside the main chamber, there's a dedicated conditioning area with baffles, housing essential components like heaters and cooling coils. These elements play a crucial role in air conditioning.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

224 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Uniform Temperature: Conditioned air is introduced into the main chamber to ensure consistent temperature distribution throughout the workspace, maintaining a stable temperature environment during tests.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

225 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(7)/Pg 14 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

226 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 36 0 R/Pg 15 0 R>>
endobj

227 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Laminar Airflow: The chamber is designed for laminar airflow, achieved using a fan motor and impeller with an appropriate capacity. This setup guarantees even distribution of temperature and humidity within the chamber, adhering to specified limits.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

228 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Motor Shaft: The motor shaft used for chamber air circulation is constructed with SS 304 without any joints. The motor is positioned outside the chamber, while an extended-length SS 304 shaft drives the fans. This design ensures smooth and reliable operation while preserving the chamber's internal environment.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

229 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Motor Winding: For high-temperature chambers, we utilize motor windings of H class, whereas for chambers operating below 130\260C, F class motor windings are employed.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

230 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(These features combine to create an efficient and precise air circulation system within the climatic test chamber, facilitating accurate and dependable test conditions for various experiments and applications.)/E(These features combine to create an efficient and precise air circulation system within the climatic test chamber, facilitating accurate and dependable test conditions for various experiments and applications.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

231 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(INCONEL-TYPE AIR HEATERS WITH PTFE WIRE AND SILICON END CAP)/E(INCONEL-TYPE AIR HEATERS WITH PTFE WIRE AND SILICON END CAP)/Pg 15 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

232 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Heating System: The chamber is equipped with sealed inconel tube heaters to maintain a uniform temperature. These heaters are meticulously designed to ensure even heat distribution throughout the chamber. Heat input is regulated by solid-state relays, controlled through a PLC with a PID controller programmer.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

233 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(One notable advantage of inconel tube heaters is their exceptional ability to withstand high temperatures and corrosive environments. Inconel, known for its outstanding durability and heat resistance, is well-suited for prolonged use in challenging conditions.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

234 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 36 0 R/Pg 15 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

235 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Compared to stainless steel heaters, inconel heaters exhibit superior resistance to oxidation, corrosion, and high-temperature degradation. They are engineered to deliver reliable and efficient heat transfer without direct radiation onto the test item, ensuring a uniform heating process that doesn't adversely affect the test specimen.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

236 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(In conclusion, the use of sealed inconel tube heaters is highly recommended for maintaining precise and uniform chamber temperatures while ensuring the long-term performance and durability of the heating system.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

237 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(OUR CHAMBER'S REFRIGERATION SYSTEM IS DESIGNED FOR OPTIMAL PERFORMANCE)/E(OUR CHAMBER'S REFRIGERATION SYSTEM IS DESIGNED FOR OPTIMAL PERFORMANCE)/Pg 15 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

238 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 409 0 R/ActualText(Single-stage compressor for temperatures up to -40\260C, and a double-stage compressor for temperatures below -70\260C. We select our compressors from reputable brands like Bitzer, Dorin, Bock, Danfoss, SECOP, or Embraco.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

239 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 410 0 R/ActualText(Environmentally friendly refrigerants are used, with R404A for single-compressor systems and R404A/R23 for cascade systems.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

240 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 411 0 R/ActualText(Safety features include HP/LP cut-off switches, pressure transmitters for continuous monitoring, and suction line temperature sensors for enhanced safety.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

241 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(8)/Pg 15 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

242 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 37 0 R/Pg 16 0 R>>
endobj

243 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 412 0 R/ActualText(The system can have a water or air-cooled condenser based on the model. Temperature monitoring and safety limits are integrated into our PLC system for effective control and protection.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

244 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 413 0 R/ActualText(The compressor and condenser unit are positioned below the chamber for optimal performance.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

245 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 37 0 R/Pg 16 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

246 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 414 0 R/ActualText(For condenser cooling, our PLC system monitors the air or water inlet temperature. If it exceeds 26\260C \(water\) or 40\260C \(air\), a safety alarm triggers, and chamber operation stops until the temperature returns to normal, which can be adjusted through HMI and PC software. This setup ensures efficient cooling and temperature control for our thermal cyclic test chamber.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

247 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Our test chamber's instrumentation includes a Siemens S7 1200 PLC and a custom-designed HMI by Proface, Weintek, or SESS. The HMI boasts a 7" touchscreen with segment 100 functionality, allowing for programming and profiling of up to 10 cycles with a maximum of 999 repetitions, catering to customer RFQ requests.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

248 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Furthermore, we offer an alternative model equipped with a PC-based control system. Our PLC communicates seamlessly with PC LabVIEW software through Ethernet TCP/IP. This LabVIEW-based software, known as SESS Climatic Test Viewer, operates without the need for a license, requiring only a free runtime engine. It also offers unlimited storage capabilities for programming and control log files.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

249 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(To ensure precise temperature measurement and control, we employ PT100 temperature sensors of class A type. The HMI simplifies programming and control of the test chamber.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

250 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Additionally, chamber operation can be carried out via PC software. For PC-based control, the following requirements apply \(Note that if you opt for the HMI model, the PC is optional and will be provided upon your request\):)/Pg 16 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

251 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 415 0 R/ActualText(HP or Dell Desktop Computer )/Pg 16 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

252 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 416 0 R/ActualText(Processor: Intel Core i3 or higher)/Pg 16 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

253 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 417 0 R/ActualText(Memory \(RAM\): 8 GB)/Pg 16 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

254 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 418 0 R/ActualText(Internal HDD Capacity: 512 GB)/Pg 16 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

255 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 419 0 R/ActualText(Display Monitor: 21.5" FHD \(Full HD\))/Pg 16 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

256 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 420 0 R/ActualText(At least one dedicated Ethernet port for )/Pg 16 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

257 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(chamber connection and an additional Wi-Fi)/Pg 16 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

258 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Ethernet port for network connectivity.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

259 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(This combination of the PLC control system, custom HMI, and LabVIEW-based PC software offers a versatile and comprehensive solution for programming, controlling, and monitoring test chamber operations. It ensures flexibility and ease of use, facilitating efficient and precise temperature testing across various applications.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

260 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(PC Software Future )/E(PC Software Future )/Pg 16 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

261 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 421 0 R/ActualText(Test parameter Data logging )/Pg 16 0 R/K[18]>>
endobj

262 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 422 0 R/ActualText(Make a multiple Profile )/Pg 16 0 R/K[19]>>
endobj

263 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 423 0 R/ActualText(Refrigeration Performance monitor window )/Pg 16 0 R/K[20]>>
endobj

264 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 424 0 R/ActualText(DI/DO\220S status window monitoring )/Pg 16 0 R/K[21]>>
endobj

265 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 425 0 R/ActualText(Control system monitor screen to identify the working condition status of solenoid valves, pressure status and temperature display .)/Pg 16 0 R/K[22]>>
endobj

266 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(9)/Pg 16 0 R/K[23]>>
endobj

267 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 38 0 R/Pg 17 0 R>>
endobj

268 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Control Panel & Wiring: A separate control panel will be provided, attached to the main chamber, which will house the programmer, on/off switches, fuses, contactors, indicating lamps, etc. Channel type wiring will be implemented using suitable copper wires with appropriate current ratings, along with marking ferrules, crimped dowel terminals, elmex connectors, and so on.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

269 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(The electrical and instrumentation panel will be meticulously wired in compliance with international standards to ensure safety and reliability. Each electrical cable will be tagged with ID numbers, and the corresponding details will be clearly documented in the maintenance manual. Comprehensive circuit diagrams and relevant information will also be included.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

270 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(To facilitate accurate and efficient design, we utilize SolidWorks 3D software for developing our drawings. This advanced software enables us to create detailed structural and electrical drawings that adhere to industry standards and specifications. By utilizing SolidWorks, we can ensure precise and comprehensive documentation of the electrical components and wiring layout of the Thermal cyclic test chamber.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

271 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Furthermore, we take pride in mentioning that our standard test chamber has been certified by TUV and carries the CE mark. This certification validates that our Stand test chamber only complies with the essential health, safety, and environmental protection requirements of the European Union. It serves as a testament to our commitment to providing high-quality, safe, and reliable equipment.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

272 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Our dedication to utilizing modern software tools and obtaining relevant certifications reflects our unwavering commitment to delivering superior products that meet the highest industry standards and exceed customer expectations.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

273 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Solid state relays for control for dry heater.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

274 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(IN OUR CHAMBER, THE PLC \(PROGRAMMABLE LOGIC CONTROLLER\) WILL EFFICIENTLY CONTROL AND MONITOR THE FOLLOWING ASPECTS:)/E(IN OUR CHAMBER, THE PLC \(PROGRAMMABLE LOGIC CONTROLLER\) WILL EFFICIENTLY CONTROL AND MONITOR THE FOLLOWING ASPECTS:)/Pg 17 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

275 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Temperature sensors: The PLC will handle the set point temperature and continuously monitor the attained temperature values to ensure precise temperature control.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

276 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Status of compressor: The PLC will monitor the operating status of the compressor, including start/stop commands and fault detection, to ensure proper functioning of the refrigeration system.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

277 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Pressure sensors: The PLC will gather data from pressure sensors to monitor the pressure levels within the system and trigger appropriate actions based on predefined thresholds.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

278 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Valves: The PLC will control various valves in the system, such as expansion valves, solenoid valves, and safety valves, to regulate the flow of refrigerant and other fluids.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

279 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Heater: The PLC will control the operation of the heater, ensuring accurate and consistent heating as per the desired temperature profile.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

280 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Circulation Fan / Blower: The PLC will regulate the speed and operation of the circulation fan or blower to maintain proper air circulation and temperature uniformity within the chamber.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

281 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Over current / over temperature protection: The PLC will incorporate protective measures, such as overcurrent and over temperature protection, to safeguard all the above components from potential damage or malfunctions.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

282 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(By centralizing the control of these critical components, the PLC ensures efficient and reliable operation of the thermal cyclic test chamber while maintaining safety and accuracy in temperature control.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

283 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(10)/Pg 17 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

